{"id":1156,"date":"2020-11-21T06:52:19","date_gmt":"2020-11-21T14:52:19","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1156"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:44","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:44","slug":"build-the-gorilla-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-gorilla-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Build the Gorilla Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216381585d\" name=\"6a2216381585d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the shoulders<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Use four long bolts to attach one blueboard on top of two blueboards. This will give you a wider base to work with.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt four short standoffs to the blueboard base. The ends of the short L-frames that are sticking up should be facing the outer edges of the blueboards. Pay attention to their placement!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the DC motors to the short L-frames, and then flip everything upside down.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1157&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1158&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1159&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216381596e\" name=\"6a2216381596e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the feet<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Make two sets of long metal frames by attaching a 4-hole metal frame to a 10-hole metal frame.<\/li>\n<li>Make four sets of stacked standoffs and attach them to the long metal frames. Pay attention to their placement!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Two sets should be one short standoff and two long standoffs.<\/li>\n<li>Two sets should be one long standoff and one short standoff.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1160&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1161&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221638159ce\" name=\"6a221638159ce\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add the Smart Inventor Board<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt the Smart Inventor Board to the shorter stacked standoffs.<\/li>\n<li>Attach a long standoff to each bottom corner of the Smart Inventor Board.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1162&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1163&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163815a3f\" name=\"6a22163815a3f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the waist and arms<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Build two more sets of stacked standoffs with one short standoff and one long standoff for each set.<\/li>\n<li>Build two 12-hole metal frames by overlapping two 10-hole metal frames. Each set should have one hole sticking out at each end.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt these, along with a blueboard, to the standoffs around the Smart Inventor Board.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the stacked standoffs you made to the standoffs at the bottom corners of the Smart Inventor Board.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt 10-hole metal frames to two horn brackets.<\/li>\n<li>Build four sets of stacked standoffs. Each set should have two short standoffs.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the stacked standoffs to the 7th and 10th holes of the 10-hole metal frames, and then attach a 4-hole metal frame to the standoffs.<\/li>\n<li>Instead of bolting the standoff into the 10th hole on the 10-hole metal frame, use a short standoff to secure it.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1164&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1165&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163815a95\" name=\"6a22163815a95\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add the battery box<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Attach two long bolts to the battery box.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the battery box to the blueboard on top of the Smart Inventor Board.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1166&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1167&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163815ae5\" name=\"6a22163815ae5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Connect the shoulders<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Flip the wide blueboard base upside down so the motors are underneath.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the base to the stacked standoffs.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1168&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163815b36\" name=\"6a22163815b36\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add the arms<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Attach the horn brackets to the motors with black screws.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the wheels to the standoffs at the end of each arm.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1169&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1170&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163815b90\" name=\"6a22163815b90\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wire the Gorilla Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To wire your Gorilla Bot, place it so the Smart Inventor Board is facing you.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The motor on your right is M1.<\/li>\n<li>The motor on your left is M2.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the motors to their respective spots on the Smart Inventor Board (M1, M2, M3, and M4 are all marked).<\/li>\n<li>Make sure that the red wires are the in the negative position (facing the inside) and that the black wires are in the positive position (facing the outside)!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1171&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163815bdc\" name=\"6a22163815bdc\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This video shows how the Gorilla Bot works![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=67PUv0TVq0U&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 10 Build the shoulders [vc_column_text] Use four long bolts to attach one blueboard on top of two blueboards. This will give you a wider base to work with.&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-gorilla-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1744,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1753,1777,1793,1617,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2168,2200,2172,2171],"class_list":["post-1156","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-gorilla-bot","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","module-gorilla","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1156","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1156\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1172,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1156\/revisions\/1172"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1744"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1156"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1156"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1156"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\